# Vapi Studio best practices

When editing Vapi Studio or a project under `projects/`:

1. Read `docs/best-practices/README.md` and the matching guide.
2. Also `agent/AGENTS.md`.
3. Enforce: **one CTA per turn**; **conversations must end** (`limits.maxTurns` / `limits.maxDurationMs`, defaults 40 / 20m — never unlimited); fail-closed constrained extracts; short digit listen timeouts; never store ASR junk as PII; **at most one spoken first name per turn**; **soft affirmatives on multi-choice → local re-ask** (not Brain/unknown); **silent handoffs** (no filler restating the last beat); **mad: one re-engage then transfer** (do not reason with angry callers more than once — nodes-and-listens.md); **no speaking raw userText / off-topic LLM output** (brain-and-prompt-injection.md); **no speaking node/transition/event names or graph state** (conversation-design.md § Human-like UX); **analytics funnel catalogs in code** (stamp tags only; no `payload.funnels`); **logs/events must explain the call**; update the matching doc layer in the same change (`docs/reference/runtime-api.md` for contracts).

Projects mirror this via `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/…` and `.cursor/rules/vapi-studio-best-practices.mdc` (from package postinstall).
